      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "After reviewing the feasibility, I stand by the high-priority directive to switch to HCHM to safeguard against severe solar activity. Aestivation mode for the High-Res Spectrometer and Sub-Surface Radar is achievable, albeit with reduced operational suite. Essential sensors will continue to perform, ensuring mission success and granting us the reprieve necessary to survive the full extent of the solar event. Please focus on securing shipboard integrity above all else. Data downlink from any remaining operational instruments, while less comprehensive, will still yield valuable information for future analysis. Captain, rest assured that our adherence to the HCHM protocol, while visually interrupting our scientific aspirations, enacts the broader strategic imperative to stabilize our systems and ensure our crew's survival and the ongoing viability of our expeditionary objectives.",
